    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_bBeKZ8gvO8uMoo6",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID161",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "The musician As Sam strolled down the empty street, his stomach growled, reminding him that he ha...",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<b>The musician<br><br></b>\n<p>As Sam strolled down the empty street, his stomach growled, reminding him that he hadn’t eaten all day. He passed by a corner where John, a street musician, usually played. They would say hello and often exchange a few words. Tonight, though, John was sprawled against the wall, sound asleep. Sam’s gaze shifted to the plate near him. Some coins were in it, but fewer than usual. Sam pondered: not a good day for the two of us.<br>\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>He hadn’t finished the thought that a dilemma came to his mind. Should he leave a few of his own coins as a small gesture for someone who might need it even more than he did? Or should he take just a little from the plate, enough to buy a sandwich and appease his hunger?</p>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "QuestionType": "DB",
        "Selector": "TB",
        "DataVisibility": {
          "Private": false,
          "Hidden": false
        },
        "Configuration": {
          "QuestionDescriptionOption": "UseText"
        },
        "QuestionDescription": "The musician As Sam strolled down the empty street, his stomach growled, reminding him that he ha...",
        "ChoiceOrder": [],
        "Validation": {
          "Settings": {
            "Type": "None"
          }
        },
        "GradingData": [],
        "Language": [],
        "NextChoiceId": 4,
        "NextAnswerId": 1,
        "DisplayLogic": {
          "0": {
            "0": {
              "Description": "<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If</span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">story2</span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to</span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 1 </span>",
              "LeftOperand": "story2",
              "LogicType": "EmbeddedField",
              "Operator": "EqualTo",
              "RightOperand": "1",
              "Type": "Expression"
            },
            "Type": "If"
          },
          "Type": "BooleanExpression",
          "inPage": false
        },
        "QuestionText_Unsafe": "As Sam wandered down the deserted street, his stomach churned with an empty ache, each step a reminder of the meals he’d skipped. The night was quiet, and this was a familiar route. He paused at the corner where a street musician usually played lively tunes. Tonight, though, the scene was different.<br><br>The musician was slumped against the brick wall, his head tilted, his chest rising and falling in the rhythm of deep sleep. At his feet was a battered plate, piled high with coins and a few crumpled bills—the rewards of his music, painstakingly earned through the kindness of passersby.<br><br>Sam’s eyes lingered on the plate, his heart pounding as the conflict rose within him. Just a few coins, he thought. Enough to buy a sandwich and quiet the gnawing hunger. The musician wouldn’t even notice. His fingers inched closer to the plate, trembling with hesitation. The thought clawed at his conscience: was it really right to take from someone who likely needed it as much as he did? The choice felt extremely heavy for something so small—a bite to eat, a moment’s relief. But small things, he realized, could ripple into something far greater.<br><br>His hand froze in midair, caught between hunger and the reluctance to take.",
        "DataExportTag": "Q161",
        "QuestionID": "QID161"
      }
    },
    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_bBeKZ8gvO8uMoo6",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID162",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "The inheritance   When his father’s inheritance was first divided, Bob was surprised not to recei",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<b>The inheritance</b><br />\n&nbsp;\n<p>When his father&rsquo;s inheritance was first divided, Bob was surprised not to receive the lake house, given its special emotional significance to him. Unexpectedly, though, while searching for an old picture on his father&rsquo;s desk, Bob found a more recent version of the will, bequeathing to him the lake house, where Bob and his father spent many weekends sharing their passion for fishing. To his surprise, he also found a letter from Tom, telling their dad about his financial struggles. Bob was aware of his brother&rsquo;s bad financial situation, but he did not know he was in such dire straits.<br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Faced with the reality of the mistake, Bob wondered: should he take from Tom the house he was entitled to and honor his father&rsquo;s true wishes, which would restore the fairness of the inheritance? Or should he leave things as they were and offer to help Tom with his debt?</p>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "QuestionType": "DB",
        "Selector": "TB",
        "DataVisibility": {
          "Private": false,
          "Hidden": false
        },
        "Configuration": {
          "QuestionDescriptionOption": "UseText"
        },
        "QuestionDescription": "The inheritance   When his father’s inheritance was first divided, Bob was surprised not to recei...",
        "ChoiceOrder": [],
        "Validation": {
          "Settings": {
            "Type": "None"
          }
        },
        "GradingData": [],
        "Language": [],
        "NextChoiceId": 4,
        "NextAnswerId": 1,
        "DisplayLogic": {
          "0": {
            "0": {
              "Description": "<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If</span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">story2</span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to</span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 2 </span>",
              "LeftOperand": "story2",
              "LogicType": "EmbeddedField",
              "Operator": "EqualTo",
              "RightOperand": "2",
              "Type": "Expression"
            },
            "Type": "If"
          },
          "Type": "BooleanExpression",
          "inPage": false
        },
        "QuestionText_Unsafe": "When the inheritance was divided, the brothers, Bob and Tom, went their separate ways, each carrying the weight of their memories and the futures they hoped to build. Time passed quietly until Bob, sorting through an old box of family documents, stumbled upon a forgotten addendum to their father’s will. His hands trembled as he read the faded lines that revealed a truth he hadn’t known: their father had intended for Bob to inherit the lake house—a place woven deeply into his happiest memories. <br><br>The lake house had been their sanctuary, the backdrop of countless weekends, where their father had taught Bob to tie fishing knots and told stories of his own boyhood adventures. When the estate had been divided, Bob had been puzzled that such a meaningful place wasn’t left to him. He’d assumed it was because Tom, struggling financially, needed it more, and he hadn’t questioned the fairness of the arrangement.<br><br> Now, holding the evidence of his father’s true intentions, Bob felt the weight of a difficult choice. Should he assert his claim, risking the fragile peace between him and Tom, or let things remain as they were, sparing his brother any potential resentment? As he gazed out his window, Bob felt the weight between asserting his right versus letting things as they stood.<br>",
        "DataExportTag": "Q162",
        "QuestionID": "QID162"
      }
    },
    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_bBeKZ8gvO8uMoo6",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID163",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "The lottery   Two friends, Mike and Jack, stopped by a convenience store on their way home, each...",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<b>The lottery</b><br>\n&nbsp;\n<p>Two friends, Mike and Jack, stopped by a convenience store on their way home, each deciding to buy a lottery ticket on a whim. They then casually agreed to check their tickets later and touch base if either of them got lucky. When Mike later checked at the 10 digits, he was stunned to see he had won a significant prize. He was happy but also thought about his friend, feeling as though luck had stemmed from a shared experience.<br><br></p>\n\n<p>He wrestled with what to do. Should he call Tom to share the news and possibly offer a portion of the winnings as a goodwill gesture? Or should he just keep the prize, given that the tickets were clearly individually purchased?&nbsp;After all, he would not be taking anything from Jake, only keeping his winnings.</p>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "QuestionType": "DB",
        "Selector": "TB",
        "DataVisibility": {
          "Private": false,
          "Hidden": false
        },
        "Configuration": {
          "QuestionDescriptionOption": "UseText"
        },
        "QuestionDescription": "The lottery   Two friends, Mike and Jack, stopped by a convenience store on their way home, each...",
        "ChoiceOrder": [],
        "Validation": {
          "Settings": {
            "Type": "None"
          }
        },
        "GradingData": [],
        "Language": [],
        "NextChoiceId": 4,
        "NextAnswerId": 1,
        "DisplayLogic": {
          "0": {
            "0": {
              "Description": "<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If</span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">story2</span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to</span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 3 </span>",
              "LeftOperand": "story2",
              "LogicType": "EmbeddedField",
              "Operator": "EqualTo",
              "RightOperand": "3",
              "Type": "Expression"
            },
            "Type": "If"
          },
          "Type": "BooleanExpression",
          "inPage": false
        },
        "QuestionText_Unsafe": "On their way home, Bob and Tom had stopped at a convenience store, bantering about their bad luck with lotteries. Tom had suggested they each buy a ticket, a whim sparked by the colorful display near the counter. Bob had hesitated, but Tom’s grin and a lighthearted quip about winning millions made him reach for his wallet. They left the store chuckling, the tickets tucked carelessly into their pockets, and promised to check them the next day.<br><br>The next morning, Bob sat frozen at his kitchen table, the ticket trembling in his hand. The numbers stared back at him, unmistakable and life-changing. He’d won—a prize so substantial that the thought of it felt unreal, like a dream he hadn’t quite woken from. For a moment, his mind spun with possibilities: the debts he could pay off, the future he could secure. But the thrill was soon dampened by a quiet, insistent voice in the back of his mind: Tom.<br><br>It was Tom’s idea to stop. Tom’s playful nudge had led him to buy the ticket in the first place. Without that moment, without his friend’s suggestion, he wouldn’t be holding a fortune in his hands. They had each paid with their own money, yes, and their tickets were separate. Still, the moment—the chance—felt like it belonged to both of them. <br><br>Bob stared at his phone, the screen dark and waiting. Should he call Tom and share the news? Would it feel right to keep the winnings entirely for himself? Maybe offering a portion would honor the shared spark of luck. But then again, wasn’t the prize technically his alone? The rules were clear, weren’t they? As the coffee in his mug grew cold, Bob wrestled with the decision, torn between the elation of his win and the weight of doing what might be fair. <br>",
        "DataExportTag": "Q163",
        "QuestionID": "QID163"
      }
    },
    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_bBeKZ8gvO8uMoo6",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID164",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "A personal successAfter weeks of intense preparation, Steve was thrilled to receive a well-deserv...",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<b>A personal success</b><p></p>After weeks of intense preparation, Steve was thrilled to receive a well-deserved performance bonus at work for exceeding his sales target. The recognition felt satisfying—a tangible reward for the long hours he’d poured into his work and the many nights he’d stayed late fine-tuning his pitch. <br><br>But as he celebrated, he couldn’t shake a lingering thought. A close coworker, Max, had stepped in during a pivotal moment, helping Steve close the deal that pushed him over the target. At the time, Max had brushed it off, calling it “just a quick tip.” <br><br>Steve struggled with what to do. Should he give part of his bonus to Max as a gesture of appreciation? Or should he keep it for himself, given that it had been awarded to him alone based on his sustained hard work? After all, he would not be taking anything from Max, only keeping what he earned. The bonus was in fact awarded solely for individual performance and, given the standard practice at the company, there was no expectation of sharing. <p></p>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "QuestionType": "DB",
        "Selector": "TB",
        "DataVisibility": {
          "Private": false,
          "Hidden": false
        },
        "Configuration": {
          "QuestionDescriptionOption": "UseText"
        },
        "QuestionDescription": "A personal successAfter weeks of intense preparation, Steve was thrilled to receive a well-deserv...",
        "ChoiceOrder": [],
        "Validation": {
          "Settings": {
            "Type": "None"
          }
        },
        "GradingData": [],
        "Language": [],
        "NextChoiceId": 4,
        "NextAnswerId": 1,
        "DisplayLogic": {
          "0": {
            "0": {
              "Description": "<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If</span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">story2</span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Equal to</span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 4 </span>",
              "LeftOperand": "story2",
              "LogicType": "EmbeddedField",
              "Operator": "EqualTo",
              "RightOperand": "4",
              "Type": "Expression"
            },
            "Type": "If"
          },
          "Type": "BooleanExpression",
          "inPage": false
        },
        "QuestionText_Unsafe": "After weeks of relentless effort, Bob felt a rush of pride as he received the email confirming his bonus. He’d done it. The recognition wasn’t just a number on his paycheck—it was validation of the long hours, the missed dinners, and the late nights spent refining every detail of his sales pitch. Sitting at his desk, he allowed himself a rare moment to bask in the satisfaction of a job well done. <br><br>But as the initial excitement settled, a shadow of doubt crept in. His thoughts turned to Tom, the coworker, who once helped Bob during his campaign. It had been a brief exchange—Tom had leaned over, glanced at the figures, and suggested a subtle tweak to Bob’s pitch. “Just a quick tip,” Tom had said with a shrug, brushing off any thanks. Yet that tip probably helped Bob reach the target.<br><br>Bob frowned, drumming his fingers on the desk. Would keeping the entire bonus feel right? Should he share a portion as a gesture of gratitude, even if Tom hadn’t asked for or expected it? Bob leaned back in his chair, torn between the pride for his effortful achievement and the thought about acknowledging the role others had played.<br>",
        "DataExportTag": "Q164",
        "QuestionID": "QID164"
      }
    },
