        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>The Mutual Aid Gift&nbsp;</strong></p>\n\n<p>James and his friend Mark had both been going through a rough financial patch. They often talked about ways to make ends meet, and neither of them had much savings left. One morning, James received an unexpected email from a local charity organization he had applied to months ago. “Congratulations! You have been selected for financial assistance. You will be receiving the full aid amount to help with your expenses.”&nbsp;<br><br></p>\n\n<p>Mark, who had applied for the same program, wasn’t selected. Even though they were in similar situations, James was the only one who received the funds.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><br></p>\n\n<p>Now James faced a choice. The money was his, and there was no expectation to share. But he also knew Mark was struggling just as much. Should he give some of the money to Mark? And if so, how much?&nbsp;</p>",
