    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_bBeKZ8gvO8uMoo6",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID197",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "The Mutual Aid Gift  James and his friend Mark had both been going through a rough financial patc..",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>The Mutual Aid Gift&nbsp;</strong></p>\n\n<p>James and his friend Mark had both been going through a rough financial patch. They often talked about ways to make ends meet, and neither of them had much savings left. One morning, James received an unexpected email from a local charity organization he had applied to months ago. “Congratulations! You have been selected for financial assistance. You will be receiving the full aid amount to help with your expenses.”<br>\n<br>\nMark had applied for the same program, but received absolutely nothing. James got everything. The allocation, due only to luck, felt very unfair. Mark was struggling. James was tempted to give some of the aid to Mark. There was no expectation to share, but could he really keep it all to himself while his friend Mark had nothing?</p>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "Q197",
        "QuestionType": "DB",
        "Selector": "TB",
        "DataVisibility": {
          "Private": false,
          "Hidden": false
        },
        "Configuration": {
          "QuestionDescriptionOption": "UseText"
        },
        "QuestionDescription": "The Mutual Aid Gift  James and his friend Mark had both been going through a rough financial patc...",
        "DisplayLogic": {
