    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_bBeKZ8gvO8uMoo6",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID198",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "The Mutual Aid Gift James had been going through a rough financial patch. He had trouble making e...",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>The Mutual Aid Gift</strong></p>\n\n<p>James had been going through a rough financial patch. He had trouble making ends meet, and did not have much savings left. One morning, James received an unexpected email from a local charity organization for an aid program he had applied to months ago. “Congratulations! You have been selected for assistance. You will be receiving financial aid to help with your expenses.”<br>\n<br>\nAs he went to collect, he got to know Mark, who was struggling like him but obtained zero aid. James wondered whether he should give something to him, but saw downsides. The process for allocating the aid was fair, he did not take anything from Mark. Also, he barely knew him, so there was no expectation to share. How could he give money to a stranger given that he needed it?</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "Q198",
        "QuestionType": "DB",
        "Selector": "TB",
        "DataVisibility": {
          "Private": false,
          "Hidden": false
        },
