      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID202",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "The Team Leader After weeks of intense preparation, Steve was thrilled to learn that his team was...",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<b>The Team Leader</b>\n<p>After weeks of intense preparation, Steve was thrilled to learn that his team was awarded a performance bonus for exceeding their sales target. The recognition felt satisfying&mdash;a tangible reward for the long hours he&#39;d poured into work and the many nights he&#39;d stayed late fine-tuning his pitch. The director called Steve to discuss the bonus and said: &quot;You guys did great. Since you are the team leader, the usual split is for you to get 70% of the bonus and for Max to get 30%. However, the final decision is yours, and you may increase or decrease your share.&quot; &nbsp;<br />\n<br />\nWhen deciding, Steve could not avoid thinking that Max, who was recently hired, had been inconsistent throughout the project, often leaving early or focusing on simple tasks. Steve could stick with the usual split. Or he could take from Max&rsquo;s 30%, arguing that his leadership and effort justified a bigger share. But he could also choose to give Max a larger portion, knowing that Max&#39;s contribution&mdash;though small&mdash;had come at a crucial moment. What should he do?</p>",
